+
+## Deployment contract
+
+The approval Linux account is a separate security principal. Never expose its desktop, login password, private key, Xauthority or session to ordinary desk users, browser or remote-control tools. The deployment administrator must review seat isolation; no general desktop, auto-login, remote desktop or shared X server is supported. Use an actual local LightDM X11 session on a dedicated seat/approval host, not Xvfb, synthetic logind records, a transient systemd service or a spoofed DISPLAY. The approval account must have a private administrator-provisioned 0700 local home (root-controlled ancestors), an interactive shell and administrator-controlled login credential distinct from the encrypted approval passphrase. Do not change its existing UID, primary group, recovery authority or signing keys. Do not give the normal desk account the login credential or authority groups. The reviewed native recovery marker and explicit desktop opt-in remain separate.
