+From the root-owned installed source `/opt/maj-vaj`, an administrator may first run `bash scripts/provision_review_desktop.sh --check` and then explicitly `--install`. This installs the fixed Xsession entry, root-owned polkit rule (active local approval identity may start only the named review unit), protected review unit and tmpfiles definition. It does not enable the marker, start LightDM, change accounts, select a default session or alter the trading desk. Administrator must first provision and verify the dedicated session, and only then explicitly install the root-owned `/etc/maj-vaj/review-desktop-enabled` opt-in file (not part of the installer). The prior `/etc/maj-vaj/reviewed-recovery-enabled` contract continues to apply. Start a real local graphical login as the approval account and select `Maj Vaj PAPER approval` in the greeter; the session displays a review-launch button and an exit button. The launcher cannot sign or change balances. On invocation it checks actual logind session membership, unique active unlocked X11 session, immutable cookie identity and X server access control, then invokes the unchanged fixed systemd unit through polkit. A separate protected service owns the recovery approval window, challenge and encrypted passphrase operation. Logout retires the private copied cookie, never a newer session's cookie. No cookie values enter logs, process arguments, the project directory, the desk or any model.
