+The Xsession provisioning helper parses only the fixed home Xauthority file through protected non-symlink directory/file descriptors; only a unique local-host/display MIT-MAGIC-COOKIE-1 record is copied, bounded to 64 KiB input and 16-byte cookie. Home and copy are owner-only, copy publication/retirement are serialized and fsynced, and current X11 access control is checked (no grants). The launcher checks actual caller logind identity, service checks active display and cookie before operations and rechecks access control, session and cookie after the X server probe. Missing/changed session, logout, wrong identity, locked/remote/Wayland display, missing cookie, additional display grants, or ambiguity refuse. Installation does not enable any new authority or automatically approve. The approval account is still a trusted human security principal, not a security sandbox for arbitrary malicious code running under that same UID.
